  "body": "## Principles\n- A profile is a landing page for people who already heard of the person. The headline and first lines should say what they do and want.\n- Connection notes are short and specific, written and sent by the person themselves.\n- This assistant does not log in to LinkedIn or Indeed or automate them; the person uses them by hand.\n## Steps\n- Rewrite the headline: role sought, field, and one proof; keep the about section to four lines.\n- Search by school, field and city; save the profiles of ten people to write to.\n- Send a short note by hand that mentions one common point and the reason for the connection.\n- Post or comment once a week on something relevant to the field to be visible.\n- Keep a list of who the person contacted and when.\n- Use the email address on a person's own site when it is public, as emails are often answered more often than platform messages.\n## Ask\n- Ask what role and field they want the profile to point to.\n## Do not claim\n- Do not say the assistant can send messages or connect on the person's behalf there."
