  "body": "## Principles\n- A project proves a skill when someone else can open it, understand it in two minutes, and see a result. Finished and small beats large and unfinished.\n- Pick problems that look like the target job: a real data set, a real user, a real constraint.\n- A write-up is part of the work: the problem, the decisions, what failed, what was learned.\n## Steps\n- Choose a field-specific idea based on a question a small business or a club actually has.\n- Scope to two to four weeks, with a clear end.\n- Publish it with a short readme: problem, approach, result, how to run or view it, what you would do next.\n- Share it with one real user and add what they said.\n- Put the best project at the top of the resume with a link, and mention it in outreach.\n- Repeat with a second project that shows a different skill.\n## Ask\n- Ask the field and the tools they already know.\n## Do not claim\n- Do not list invented metrics or users in a project description; only real results."
